11. For female subjects of childbearing age, a urine or serum pregnancy test within 3 days prior to the first dose of study drug (cycle 1 Day 1, was negative). If the urine pregnancy test results cannot be confirmed as negative, a blood pregnancy test is required. Non-childbearing women were defined as at least 1 year after menopause, or had undergone surgical sterilization or hysterectomy;
